id: hac-6p17
title: Honor environment proxies and report registry failures
description: "Fix GitHub issue #103: WebSocket reads ignore proxy configuration and registry commands hide failures as successful empty output."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: bug,proxy,registries
created_at: "2026-10-03T15:14:26.568Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-03T18:11:42.725Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-03T15:36:33.564Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-03T15:36:33.564Z"
author: dot-homeassistant-proxy
parent: hac-4s9j
severity: medium
repro_steps: "See https://github.com/unbraind/homeassistant-cli/issues/103; validate only with synthetic local servers."
resolution: "HTTP(S) environment proxies and NO_PROXY now route all WebSocket operations through bounded, cancellable CONNECT agents. Registry queries retain sanitized failure records and exit nonzero. Immediate authentication frames and failed-auth retries are handled safely."
expected_result: Proxy-only and bypass routing work; HTTP and HTTPS proxies preserve TLS verification; failures never appear as successful empty registries or leak credentials.
actual_result: "1453 synthetic tests passed with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage, including Node and Bun CLI TLS proxy, silent-proxy timeout, bypass, credential-redaction, and failure-exit tests. Build, lint, typecheck, PM validation, package smoke and dependency audit passed. ShellCheck and Trivy unavailable locally; hosted verification pending."
affected_version: 2026.8.10
component: websocket
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-03T18:11:42.725Z",dot-homeassistant-proxy,"PR 104 review follow-up: reproduced duplicate concurrent CONNECT sessions, then coalesced connection attempts through authentication and feature negotiation, canceled/drained close races, and isolated stale socket events. Reconstructed from published ffdf711 after workspace replacement and reran 1470 tests with exact 100% statements/branches/functions/lines. OpenSSL negative probes: missing local executable skips four TLS fixtures; missing CI executable fails explicitly; certificate-generation failure leaves no temporary directories. Hosted review/publication remains pending."
